---
// /en/privacy — EN mirror of /de/datenschutz/.
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
	lang="en"
	title="Privacy Policy — KI einfach verstehen"
	description="Privacy policy for KI einfach verstehen: what data is processed, where it lives, and how to object."
	otherLangHref="/de/datenschutz/"
	heading="Privacy Policy"
>
	<section>
		<h2>Data controller</h2>
		<p>The data controller within the meaning of the GDPR is Silvio Lindstedt und Maik Gräfendorf, GbR. For address and contact details, see the <a href="/en/legal-notice/">Legal Notice</a>.</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Principle</h2>
		<p>
			This website is static: there is no backend, no user accounts, and no cookies. The only processing of
			personal data on a server takes place via a self-hosted, cookie-free web analytics service (Matomo, see
			below). Some settings and your reading progress are additionally stored exclusively in your browser — more on
			that under "Local storage". Beyond that, there is no further tracking and no embedded third-party services
			that collect personal data.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Web analytics (Matomo)</h2>
		<p>
			This website uses the self-hosted web analytics software Matomo (endpoint: matomo.silvio-und-maik.de) to
			produce aggregated, statistical evaluations of how the site is used. The analysis is data-economical and runs
			entirely first-party on an own server. On each page access, the following technical characteristics are
			recorded: an anonymised IP address (truncated to 2 bytes before storage), browser type and version, the
			operating system reported by the browser, the device type (desktop, tablet or smartphone), the screen
			resolution, the configured browser language, the country of origin and region (geometrically derived from the
			IP address), the referrer (the page from which this website was accessed), and the subpages visited with time
			spent and time of visit. In addition, anonymous event counters are recorded for individual, voluntary
			interactions — for example your feedback on whether a lesson was helpful ("Was this lesson helpful?" at the
			end of every lesson). These counters, too, are aggregated and cannot be linked to a person.
		</p>
		<p>
			No cookies are set and no information is stored on or read from your device; because tracking is cookieless
			and IP-anonymised, no consent — and therefore no cookie banner — is required under § 25 TDDDG. There is no
			profiling, no cross-device tracking, and no sharing with third parties. The data is used exclusively for
			aggregated statistics and cannot be linked to individuals. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest
			in needs-driven development of this website). You may object to this processing at any time (Art. 21 GDPR) —
			tick the opt-out option in the field below.
		</p>
		<div id="matomo-opt-out"></div>
		<script
			is:inline
			src="https://matomo.silvio-und-maik.de/index.php?module=CoreAdminHome&action=optOutJS&divId=matomo-opt-out&language=en&showIntro=1"
		></script>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Hosting (GitHub Pages)</h2>
		<p>
			This website is hosted via GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub Inc. (88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. St., San Francisco,
			CA 94107, USA), a subsidiary of Microsoft Corporation. When you visit this website, GitHub automatically
			records the following data: IP address, browser type and version, referrer URL, and time of access.
		</p>
		<p>
			This is technically necessary for operating the website. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate
			interest). GitHub processes this data according to the{' '}
			<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
				GitHub Privacy Statement
			</a>. To safeguard the data transfer to the US, {' '}
			<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-data-protection-agreement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
				Standard Contractual Clauses (SCC)
			</a>{' '}
			under Art. 46(2)(c) GDPR are in place.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Local storage</h2>
		<p>
			This website stores a few settings exclusively in your browser (localStorage): your preferred text size,
			which lessons you have already read (for the progress indicator), and whether you have already given
			feedback on a lesson (so you aren't asked again). This data never leaves your device, is never transmitted
			to any server, and cannot be linked to a person. You can delete it at any time through your browser
			settings.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>External links</h2>
		<p>
			This website contains links to external services, notably to the open-source GitHub repository of this
			website. Clicking these links takes you away from this website. The respective provider is responsible for
			data processing on the linked pages. The star count shown in the footer and at the end of every lesson is
			fetched server-side when the website is built (GitHub Actions), not from your browser when you visit — no
			data about you is sent to GitHub in the process.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Your rights</h2>
		<p>
			You have the right to access, rectification, erasure, and restriction of processing of your personal data,
			as well as the right to data portability and to object (Art. 15–21 GDPR). Insofar as the web analytics
			(Matomo) processes personal data, you may object to it (see the web analytics section above). For questions
			about processing by GitHub (hosting), please contact{' '}
			<a href="https://support.github.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Support</a> directly.
			You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR).
		</p>
	</section>
</LegalLayout>
